Prepared Notes

1. What is Next.js?
Next.js is a React framework created by Vercel.
It makes building modern web applications easier by adding powerful features on top of React.
Simple definition:
Next.js = React + Built-in routing + Server-side features + Optimization

2. Why use Next.js? (Advantages)



FeatureBenefitFile-based RoutingNo need to install React RouterServer-Side Rendering (SSR)Better SEO and faster first loadStatic Site Generation (SSG)Extremely fast pagesAPI RoutesBackend code inside the same projectImage OptimizationAutomatic image compressionFast RefreshInstant updates while codingBuilt-in CSS & TypeScript supportEasy styling and type safety

3. Prerequisites
Before starting, make sure you have:

Node.js (version 18.17 or later recommended)
npm or yarn or pnpm
Basic knowledge of HTML, CSS, JavaScript and React
A code editor (VS Code recommended)

Check versions:
Bashnode -v
npm -v

